          "path": "_m/g/c/s/h/ballyhornan-wp/abandoned-cottage-and-a-dog-on.jpg",
          "filename": "Abandoned cottage and a dog on Rocks Road - geograph.org.uk - 1533916.jpg",
          "caption": "Abandoned cottage and a dog on Rocks Road Ballyhornan appears to be a paradise for elderly dogs. Obviously they had not heard of Stormont's plan to raise the dog licence fee by 1000% from £5 to £50 per annum. The outcry from dog owners, however, was such that Agriculture Minister, Michelle Gildernew, Sinn Fein, promptly revised her plans, and instead raising the licence fee to £12.50 for those dogs whose owners are under the age of 65. Last time I paid for a dog licence it was 37.5p.",
          "alt": "Abandoned cottage and a dog on Rocks Road Ballyhornan appears to be a paradise for elderly dogs. Obviously they had not heard of Stormont's plan to raise the dog licence fee by 1000% from £5 to £50 per annum. The outcry from dog owners, however, was such that Agriculture Minister, Michelle Gildernew, Sinn Fein, promptly revised her plans, and instead raising the licence fee to £12.50 for those dogs whose owners are under the age of 65. Last time I paid for a dog licence it was 37.5p.",
          "width": 640,
